  "base_commit": "755b2327742b6fd2780ed1321765ec0d892d3fcf",
  "pr_number": 4548,
  "issue_number": 487,
  "issue_title": "feat(search): add weighted ranked registry search",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\nHeyClaude registry search currently behaves like a broad substring filter. That is simple and predictable, but it makes API, MCP, and Raycast discovery weaker as the registry grows. We should add deterministic weighted ranking so exact title/slug/category/tag/platform matches appear before loose description matches.\n\n## Current state\n\n- Website search flows through `apps/web/src/app/api/registry/search/route.ts`.\n- Shared filtering lives in `apps/web/src/lib/api/registry-search-filters.ts`.\n- MCP search currently has its own filter path in `packages/mcp/src/registry.js`.\n- Search uses normalized haystack substring matching, with no score, ranking reason, tokenization, or typo/synonym support.\n\n## Desired behavior\n\n- Return ranked results with stable deterministic scoring.\n- Weight exact slug/title/category/tag/platform matches above description/author/brand matches.\n- Include optional score metadata internally or in debug/test fixtures without making the public API noisy.\n- Keep existing filters compatible: category, platform, safety/privacy notes, package trust, claim status, and source status.\n- Reuse the same ranking helper across website API and MCP search so clients do not drift.\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- Add a shared ranking helper near the registry search filter helpers or in the registry package if that becomes the better common boundary.\n- Preserve deterministic ordering for equal scores, probably by title or existing index order.\n- Consider multi-token matching, exact phrase boosts, slug/title boosts, and tag/platform boosts.\n- Keep result caps unchanged unless paired with pagination work.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Exact title/slug matches rank ahead of loose description matches.\n- Tag/platform/category matches contribute measurable rank improvements.\n- API and MCP search use the same ranking behavior or share the same helper.\n- Existing trust filters and facets continue to work.\n- Tests cover exact, partial, multi-token, tie-breaker, and filtered-search cases.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm exec vitest run tests/registry-search-facets.test.ts tests/mcp-server.test.ts`\n- `pnpm validate:openapi`\n- Add or update focused unit tests for the touched API/helper surface.\n- Run the narrow relevant validation command for the changed package or route.\n- Run `git diff --check` before opening a PR.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-07T08:13:45.000Z",
